WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.024 --> 00:00:04.555
Journal Entry: November 7, 1876, London My beautiful Mina was devastated by the news of Lucy’s death, and she

2
00:00:04.556 --> 00:00:12.070
just sat in her room and wept for days after the funeral. I was quite concerned for her well-being,

3
00:00:12.071 --> 00:00:16.816
but I hadn’t a clue what to do for her. Besides, I was still recovering from my own illness,

4
00:00:16.817 --> 00:00:23.491
and having terrible nightmares about my time in Transylvania. I was consumed with worry and nothing seemed able

5
00:00:23.492 --> 00:00:28.094
to bring me out of my depression. One day, the postman knocked on our door, and when I answered,

6
00:00:28.095 --> 00:00:37.801
he handed me a letter from Professor Van Helsing, a friend of Arthur’s, who we’d met at the funeral

7
00:00:37.802 --> 00:00:43.610
service. He wanted to set up a meeting to talk to Mina about her time with Lucy at her

8
00:00:43.611 --> 00:00:49.197
seaside home in Whitby. He was conducting a post-mortem investigation into the events leading up to her death. I

9
00:00:49.198 --> 00:00:57.705
was reluctant to bring this to my wife’s attention, considering her fragile state, but thought that she might benefit

10
00:00:57.706 --> 00:01:07.333
from a conversation with the professor. Mina agreed without hesitation; anything she could do to unravel the mystery of

11
00:01:07.334 --> 00:01:17.975
Lucy’s death would definitely make her feel more useful than she had felt during Lucy’s illness. Mina was nervous

12
00:01:17.976 --> 00:01:23.253
about meeting with Van Helsing, and after spending all day fretting over which dress to wear and what

13
00:01:23.254 --> 00:01:27.745
to serve her guest, she finally settled down a few minutes before his arrival. When he entered the front

14
00:01:27.746 --> 00:01:32.848
door, we both greeted him, and our servant took his coat. We asked him to have a seat in

15
00:01:32.849 --> 00:01:42.864
the sitting room and offered him a sandwich and tea. He gladly accepted, and after he had finished eating,

16
00:01:42.865 --> 00:01:47.404
we got down to business. He explained to us in great detail the turmoil that had occurred after the

17
00:01:47.405 --> 00:01:52.039
funeral and how Arthur had eventually put an end to Lucy’s suffering with a stake through her heart. Mina

18
00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:58.333
was too upset to respond and simply left the room in tears. I continued to ask the professor many

19
00:01:58.334 --> 00:02:02.334
