33
00:03:16.945 --> 00:03:19.349
for once and for all!" We began preparations at once. Mina went to locate Jack Seward and tell him

34
00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:32.039
and Arthur about the count, while I looked through my paperwork trying to find out any information I could

35
00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:37.047
about the shipment of coffins that my office had helped arrange. I eventually learned that they had been delivered

36
00:03:37.048 --> 00:03:42.555
to the count’s property in London. I rushed to find the doctor, Arthur, and the professor to tell

37
00:03:42.556 --> 00:03:47.698
them of my discovery. The four of us met in my sitting room and Mina was kind enough to

38
00:03:47.699 --> 00:03:52.539
offer us tea and cookies. "I’ve read many histories of vampire lore and legend," explained the professor. "I know

39
00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:58.452
they cannot come out in the sunlight because it hurts them, so we can work freely in the daylight.

40
00:03:58.453 --> 00:04:02.507
As long as the sun is up, the count will need to hide in his casket. I have an

